# ===== Range C: F_0a190 .. F_0d4bc =====
# Module lifecycle convention seen in this range: every game module has
#   <Module>_Init      (Game_InitModules, once at start)
#   <Module>_DeInit    (F_08664, once at program exit)
#   <Module>_RoundBegin(Round_InitModules, start of Round_Run)
#   <Module>_SetupForLevel (Round_SetupLevel, each level)
#   <Module>_LevelReset(F_08832, before a level restarts / next level)
#   <Module>_RoundEnd  (F_0873c, end of Round_Run)
# Many of these are empty (rts) hooks.

# ---- Input devices (end of the input module, used by Input_UpdateCursor) ----
F_0a190 Input_KeyToButton
@Input_KeyToButton Input_KeyToButton(a0 = input device, d0 = button index) : reads the
@Input_KeyToButton scancode stored at +$2e+2*index, and updates the button state byte at
@Input_KeyToButton +$2f+2*index (3 = just pressed, 1 = held, 4 = just released, 0 = up).
@Input_KeyToButton Used for keys 10/11 (puzzle / extra buttons) of joystick and mouse devices.
F_0a1f4 Input_JoystickToButtons
@Input_JoystickToButtons Input_JoystickToButtons(a0 = input device, d0.b = joystick byte) :
@Input_JoystickToButtons bit 2 -> left (+$2e), bit 3 -> right (+$30), bit 1 -> down (+$32),
@Input_JoystickToButtons bit 0 -> up (+$34), bit 7 -> fire (+$3e), each via Button_Update.
F_0a25c Input_PadToButtons
@Input_PadToButtons Input_PadToButtons(a0 = input device, d0.b = pad directions/fire, d1.w = pad buttons) :
@Input_PadToButtons like Input_JoystickToButtons (STE/Jaguar pad or TeamTap), plus bit 6 -> +$40
@Input_PadToButtons and pad word bit 13 -> +$42, bit 8 -> +$44.
F_0a2fa Input_MoveCursorByDirs
@Input_MoveCursorByDirs Input_MoveCursorByDirs(a0 = input device, d0.l = speed) : moves the cursor
@Input_MoveCursorByDirs position (+0 x, +4 y, fixed point) by d0 for each held direction button
@Input_MoveCursorByDirs (left -x, right +x, down +y, up -y). Speed is $4000 in Input_UpdateCursor.
F_0a328 Input_AnyFirePressed
@Input_AnyFirePressed d0 = Input_AnyFirePressed() : non-zero if joystick 0 or 1 fire (bit 7),
@Input_AnyFirePressed a mouse button or the Space key (scancode 57) is down. Skips the title screen.

