# ---- AI ray tracer (hand-written asm, called by the AI path map code F_0727a/F_07418) ----
# Maps: a0 = 3 layers (one per number of extra turns, 0-2) of 640 bytes:
# +0 9 row bitmasks (bit n = column n reached), +$80 9x12 byte distance map.
# a1 = level cells (header+$22). d0 = row, d1 = column, d2 = steps, d3 = turn depth.
F_0c99a AiTrace_ClearRowMasks
@AiTrace_ClearRowMasks AiTrace_ClearRowMasks(a0 = map) : clears the 9 row bitmask words (18 bytes).
F_0c9a8 AiTrace_ClearDistances
@AiTrace_ClearDistances AiTrace_ClearDistances(a0 = distance map) : fills 9x12 bytes with $ff
@AiTrace_ClearDistances (unreached).
F_0c9b8 AiTrace_StartRight
@AiTrace_StartRight AiTrace_StartRight(a0 = maps, a1 = cells, d0 = row, d1 = column) :
@AiTrace_StartRight saves all registers and traces to the right from the cell with 0 steps/turns.
F_0c9cc AiTrace_StartLeft
@AiTrace_StartLeft AiTrace_StartLeft(a0 = maps, a1 = cells, d0 = row, d1 = column) : same, to the left.
F_0c9e0 AiTrace_StartUp
@AiTrace_StartUp AiTrace_StartUp(a0 = maps, a1 = cells, d0 = row, d1 = column) : same, upwards.
F_0c9f4 AiTrace_StartDown
@AiTrace_StartDown AiTrace_StartDown(a0 = maps, a1 = cells, d0 = row, d1 = column) : same, downwards.
F_0ca08 AiTrace_Right
@AiTrace_Right AiTrace_Right(d0 row, d1 col, d2 steps, d3 turns) : walks right (wrapping) writing
@AiTrace_Right the step count where it is lower than the stored one; stops at rockets, holes,
@AiTrace_Right blocking arrows, a right wall or 144 steps. At each cell it recursively branches
@AiTrace_Right up/down (walls force the turn; free turns cost one of the 2 allowed extra turns).
F_0cafa AiTrace_Left
@AiTrace_Left AiTrace_Left(d0 row, d1 col, d2 steps, d3 turns) : same as AiTrace_Right, to the left.
F_0cbec AiTrace_Up
@AiTrace_Up AiTrace_Up(d0 row, d1 col, d2 steps, d3 turns) : same, upwards (row - 1, wraps to 8);
@AiTrace_Up branches left/right.
F_0ccf0 AiTrace_Down
@AiTrace_Down AiTrace_Down(d0 row, d1 col, d2 steps, d3 turns) : same, downwards (row + 1, wraps
@AiTrace_Down to 0); branches left/right.

