F_0d074 Sfx_LoadSamples
@Sfx_LoadSamples Sfx_LoadSamples() : unless memory is low, loads the 37 samples named in
@Sfx_LoadSamples SfxSampleNames into gSfxSamples (12 bytes: +0 data, +4 length, +8 flags),
@Sfx_LoadSamples scales their volume to 64/256 on machine type 6, sets gSfxLoaded, then
@Sfx_LoadSamples resets the request queue (Sfx_ResetQueue) and starts DMA sound.
F_0d156 Sfx_ResetQueue
@Sfx_ResetQueue Sfx_ResetQueue() : links the 16 sound request slots of gSfxQueue (20 bytes:
@Sfx_ResetQueue +0 sound, +4 priority, +6 frames left, +8 pan, +$c next, +$10 prev) into a list,
@Sfx_ResetQueue all idle; head = first slot, tail = last slot.
F_0d1c0 SfxQueue_Unlink
@SfxQueue_Unlink SfxQueue_Unlink(a0 = slot) : removes the slot from the request list.
F_0d204 SfxQueue_MoveToTail
@SfxQueue_MoveToTail SfxQueue_MoveToTail(a0 = slot) : moves the slot to the end of the list.
F_0d21c SfxQueue_InsertAfter
@SfxQueue_InsertAfter SfxQueue_InsertAfter(a0 = slot, a1 = position) : inserts after a1
@SfxQueue_InsertAfter (updates the tail).
F_0d258 SfxQueue_InsertBefore
@SfxQueue_InsertBefore SfxQueue_InsertBefore(a0 = slot, a1 = position) : inserts before a1
@SfxQueue_InsertBefore (updates the head). Keeps the list sorted by priority.
F_0d294 Sfx_DeInit
@Sfx_DeInit Sfx_DeInit() : stops DMA sound and frees its buffers (F_00252).
F_0d29c Sfx_Update
@Sfx_Update Sfx_Update() : once per frame. Plays the highest priority pending request when
@Sfx_Update a DMA channel is free (if gSfxLoaded and the sfx option are on), then counts down
@Sfx_Update every request; a request not played within 30 frames is dropped.
F_0d3c6 Sample_ScaleVolume
@Sample_ScaleVolume Sample_ScaleVolume(a0 = sample {data, length}, d0 = factor) : every signed
@Sample_ScaleVolume 8-bit sample = sample * factor / 256.
F_0d3f4 MusicPlayer_Init
@MusicPlayer_Init MusicPlayer_Init(a0 = voice set, a1 = tune) : calls entry +0 of the SNDREP
@MusicPlayer_Init player (entry +4 = L_0d408 is the Timer C tick, +8 = stop).
F_0d41e MusicPlayer_Stop
@MusicPlayer_Stop MusicPlayer_Stop() : calls the stop entry (+8) of the SNDREP player.
F_0d434 DmaSound_Unused_0d434
@DmaSound_Unused_0d434 DmaSound_Unused_0d434() : unreferenced. If STE DMA sound is idle (or its
@DmaSound_Unused_0d434 frame counter reached the end address), sets the DMA rate bits of $ff8921 to 3 (50 kHz).
